.TH RACEY 1
.SH NAME
racey \- a test of servers started on demand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B racey serve
.I name linger_ms
.br
.B racey call
.I name n max_ms
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B racey
tests servers started on demand
.RB ( "make demand-test" ).
.TP
.B serve
An on-demand server for port
.IR name :
it answers each call with its pid. When
.BR init (8)
asks "may you stop?" and it is unused, it says yes, then lingers
.I linger_ms
before ending, so calls arrive while it stops.
.TP
.B call
.I n
calls to
.IR name ,
with a random pause of up to
.I max_ms
between them. Every call must be answered; it prints how many failed,
how many servers answered and how many calls waited for a new one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR svc (8),
.BR init (8)
